plot includes data derived from the following works.

Geist (Vercel, with basement.studio) and Pretendard (Kil Hyung-jin)
  src/font/glyphs.nabi holds glyph outlines and advances of Geist Regular
  and, for Greek and some mathematical symbols, Pretendard, written by
  tools/font.py. Both fonts are under the SIL Open Font License 1.1; the
  license texts are in assets/fonts/. The subset is not named after either
  font.

Colormaps (src/colormap/tables.nabi, written by tools/colormaps.py)
  viridis, magma, inferno and plasma: Nathaniel J. Smith, Stefan van der
  Walt and (viridis) Eric Firing, released under CC0 1.0.
  cividis: Jamie R. Nunez, Christopher R. Anderton and Ryan S. Renslow,
  "Optimizing colormaps with consideration for color vision deficiency to
  enable accurate interpretation of scientific data", PLOS ONE 13(7),
  2018; the table as matplotlib ships it.
  coolwarm: the control points of Kenneth Moreland, "Diverging Color Maps
  for Scientific Visualization", 2009.
